made a protest in support of women's  right and workers rights turned violent  in cities around the world demonstrators  in Paris threw Molotov cocktails at  police four officers were hurt and in  the Pacific Northwest dozens of people  were arrested yesterday during clashes  with police John Blackstone shows us how  a rally in Oregon's largest city turned  chaotic police had to resort the so  called flashbangs to try to break up an  unruly crowd in Portland Oregon Monday  the city was forced to shut down its May  Day march after the peaceful protest to  support labor and immigration rights  turned violent anarchists clashed with  officer trashing police vehicles and  some businesses in the Washington state  capitol of Olympia police say dozens of  people dressed in black hurled rocks and  marbles there were several arrests this  is a group here that was very focused as  a group to really engage us and try to  frankly assault officers the protests  were just some of the many  demonstrations that took place across  the country from Los Angeles to Chicago  and New York  in perhaps a not-so-subtle nod to that  now-infamous Pepsi commercial some  demonstrators offered police a can of  Pepsi which in some cases wasn't so well  received  for the most part demonstrators came  together peacefully hoping to keep  attention on their primary cause I'm  here to fight for rights for rights for  workers rights for immigrants rights for  everybody everybody works for working  cause we need to be heard for CBS this  morning John Blackstone San Francisco
 

